f brain plugin is available","If not installed:","Step 3: Discover Brain Operators","List all available operators"],"name_hint":"fiftyone · 查找 · duplicates"},{"path":"skills/fiftyone-generate-data-lens-connector/SKILL.md","name":"fiftyone-generate-data-lens-connector","description":"Generate a Data Lens connector from an external database schema. Use when users want to connect an external data source (PostgreSQL, BigQuery, Databricks, MySQL, etc.) to FiftyOne Data Lens, or when they have a database schema and want to browse/import that data through the FiftyOne App.","headings":["Generate Data Lens Connector","Enterprise Notice","Key Directives","1. Schema first, code second","2. Propose the field mapping before generating","3. Use parameterized queries","4. Respect the batching contract","5. Keep it minimal","Workflow","Phase 1: Understand the Schema","Phase 2: Propose Field Mapping","Phase 3: Generate Connector","Phase 4: Validate","Phase 5: Iterate","Database-Specific Patterns","PostgreSQL","Driver: psycopg[binary]","Parameterization: %s positional"],"name_hint":"fiftyone · 生成 · 数据 · lens · 连接器"},{"path":"skills/fiftyone-issue-triage/SKILL.md","name":"fiftyone-issue-triage","description":"Triages FiftyOne GitHub issues by categorizing as fixed, won't fix, not reproducible, or still valid. Use when reviewing GitHub issues, triaging bugs, or closing stale issues in the voxel51/fiftyone repository.","headings":["FiftyOne Issue Triage","Categories","Workflow","1. Fetch Issue","2. Analyze","3. Assess Responsibility","4. Assess Value","5. Check Documentation","6. Categorize and Respond","Quick Reference","Response Tone","If User Willing to Contribute"],"name_hint":"fiftyone · issue · triage"},{"path":"skills/fiftyone-model-evaluation/SKILL.md","name":"fiftyone-model-evaluation","description":"Evaluate model predictions against ground truth using COCO, Open Images, or custom protocols. Use when computing mAP, precision, recall, confusion matrices, or analyzing TP/FP/FN examples for detection, classification, segmentation, or regression tasks.","headings":["Evaluate Model Predictions in FiftyOne","Key Directives","1. Check if dataset exists and has required fields","2. Install evaluation plugin if not available","If @voxel51/evaluation not listed:","3. Ask user for evaluation parameters","4. Launch App for evaluation operators","5. Close app when done","Workflow","Step 1: Verify Dataset and Fields","Step 2: Ensure Evaluation Plugin is Installed","Step 3: Launch App","Step 4: Run Evaluation","Step 5: View Results","Step 6: View Evaluation Patches (TP/FP/FN)","Convert to evaluation patches view","Count by type","Output: {'fn': 246, 'fp': 4131, 'tp': 986}"],"name_hint":"fiftyone · 模型 · 评测"},{"path":"skills/fiftyone-sdk-guidance/SKILL.md","name":"fiftyone-sdk-guidance","description":"Answers FiftyOne Python SDK questions with accurate, runnable code. Use when the user asks how to do something in the FiftyOne Python SDK, asks a docs question, no skill or operator covers their goal, or the agent is unsure of the correct FiftyOne method, argument, or field path while writing code — e.g. \"how do I do X in Python\", \"show me the SDK for filtering\", \"there's no operator for this, can I do it in code\", \"what's the API for embeddings\", \"write me a Python script to do Y\".","headings":["FiftyOne SDK Guidance","Key Directives","1. Always search docs first; never answer from training knowledge alone","2. Return runnable Python code, not pseudocode, and cite your source","3. For fallback scenarios, acknowledge the gap explicitly","4. If one search isn't enough, search again with a refined query","5. Never make up API method names or field paths","6. Degrade gracefully when the docs tool isn't connected","7. Offer to self-install the docs connection, don't just tell the user to do it","Complete Workflow","Step 1. Understand the user's goal","Step 2. Search the FiftyOne documentation","Step 3. Build the code response","Load or open your dataset","Filter examples, built from search result","Step 4. Explain the key methods","Step 5. Offer follow-up","Available Tools"],"name_hint":"fiftyone · sdk · guidance"},{"path":"skills/fiftyone-troubleshoot/SKILL.md","name":"fiftyone-troubleshoot","description":"Diagnose and fix common FiftyOne issues automatically. Use when a dataset disappeared, the App won't open, changes aren't saving, MongoDB errors occur, video codecs fail, notebook connectivity breaks, operators are missing, or any recurring FiftyOne pain point needs solving.","headings":["FiftyOne Troubleshoot","Overview","Prerequisites","Key Directives","1. Always explain, propose, and confirm before acting","2. Never touch user datasets — FiftyOne is the source of truth","3. Never directly manipulate MongoDB","4. Never modify config or files silently","5. Restart processes after env / config changes","6. Always verify after fixing","Workflow","Diagnostic Quick-Check","Health Check","Issue Index","Issue: Dataset Disappeared","Make an existing dataset persistent","Prevention: always create persistent datasets","Issue: App Won't Open"],"name_hint":"fiftyone · 排查"},{"path":"skills/fiftyone-voodo-design/SKILL.md","name":"fiftyone-voodo-design","description":"Build FiftyOne UIs using VOODO (@voxel51/voodo), the official React component library. Use when building plugin panels, creating interactive UIs, or styling FiftyOne applications. Fetches complete component API reference dynamically.","headings":["VOODO Design System for FiftyOne","Key Directive","Workflow","1. Fetch the reference","2. Use components and design tokens from the reference","3. Follow composition patterns","Installation","FiftyOne Patterns","Integration with FiftyOne SDK","Resources","Troubleshooting"],"name_hint":"fiftyone · voodo · 设计"},{"path":"skills/fiftyone-zoo-remote-model/SKILL.md","name":"fiftyone-zoo-remote-model","description":"Use when integrating a model into FiftyOne's remote model zoo — detection, classification, segmentation, e